M4-009 Single Long-Lived Core / Repository Ownership Contract
date: 2026-09-15
branch: dev
base: 8cc153e checkpoint: m4-local-concurrency
platform: Windows 11 x86_64 NTFS SQLite WAL
development state: UNCOMMITTED_DEVELOPMENT_TREE

ARCHITECTURE
Model A, independent shared Repository handles:
PARTIAL / IMPLEMENTATION LIMITATION.

Model B, one long-lived Core owner:
PASS on Windows focused validation.

Overall M4-009 status:
PARTIAL / INTERNAL / FOCUSED-TEST-GATED.

The Core owns Repository, MetadataStore/SQLite, CAS, Workspace filesystem
mutation, Operation lifecycle, and recovery entry. Agent Runtimes use the
external Agent protocol. Repository ownership is separate from repository
migration locking, Agent Workspace lease, Execution identity, and transport
session identity.

IMPLEMENTATION
The JSONL Core opens with Repository::open_as_core_owner.
An OS-held exclusive .pong/locks/core-owner.lock rejects a second Core and new
direct Repository handles. Ordinary embedded handles retain shared access only
when no Core owner is active. The lock is not durable domain state or a PID
file. Forced process exit releases it automatically.

